The partition function is therefore $\begin{aligned}Z_N
 &=\sum_{n+m=N}
   \frac{N!}{n!\,m!}
   e^{-\beta\mu H(n-m)}
 \notag\\
 &=\sum_{n=0}^{N}
   \binom{N}{n}
   \left(e^{-\beta\mu H}\right)^n
   \left(e^{+\beta\mu H}\right)^{N-n}.
 \end{aligned}$ Introduce $x=e^{-\beta\mu H},
 \qquad
 y=e^{+\beta\mu H}.$ The binomial theorem then completes the calculation: $\begin{aligned}Z_N
 &=\sum_{n=0}^{N}\binom{N}{n}x^n y^{N-n}
   =(x+y)^N
 \notag\\
 &=\left(e^{-\beta\mu H}+e^{+\beta\mu H}\right)^N
   =\left[2\cosh(\beta\mu H)\right]^N.
 \end{aligned}$

